Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:51:21 +0800
Subject: media: histb-vpss: deinterlace with the block's motion-adaptive mode

The deinterlacing menu stopped at Bob and Weave, so interlaced input
could only be doubled or passed through.
The block's five-field node interpolates a field from the ones around
it, and wants the field it produces, the one before it and the two after
it, plus a motion history that rotates between jobs.
Keep a ring of pictures whose slots carry the two fields of their
moment, feed the node from it, delay the output by three fields and
stamp it with the triggering field, leave a field as bob until it has
neighbours on both sides, and refuse windows, 4:2:2, packed input,
sharpening, flips and turns; the interpolation parameters are the
block's own defaults.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 2 files changed, 406 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)


